infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Where to store the idempotency key
  desc Postgres (durable, authoritative) vs Redis+TTL (fast hot path)
  compares
    - label Postgres table
      children
        - label ACID-durable
          desc Key inserted in the charge transaction — survives a crash
        - label Authoritative
          desc System of record for payment liability
        - label expires_at sweep
          desc Daily cleanup; Stripe v1 24h, v2 30 days
    - label Redis with TTL
      children
        - label SETNX EX, atomic
          desc Set-if-not-exists in one op — higher throughput
        - label Async-fsync risk
          desc A crash within ms can drop the entry
        - label Read-through cache
          desc Fronts Postgres; a miss falls back to the table
theme
  palette #6366f1 #f59e0b
